# One folder per client and use case: <client-slug>/<use-case-slug>/, the Nebula working folder
# every cloud session for that use case loads at its start and pushes back at its end.
# Kept: Demo Studio's studio/ (state, profile, documents, solution.json), Nebula's specs/, plans/,
# docs/, records/ (records/solution.json binds the folder to its solution), .nebula/, memory.md,
# CLAUDE.md. Left out: caches Nebula rebuilds from the tenant (entities/, entity-manifests/),
# session scratch (.sessions/), a code app checkout (<appId>/, a git repository of its own whose
# source Code Builder keeps), and anything else, such as the collateral kit's tools.
/*/*/*
!/*/*/studio/
!/*/*/specs/
!/*/*/plans/
!/*/*/docs/
!/*/*/records/
!/*/*/.nebula/
!/*/*/memory.md
!/*/*/CLAUDE.md
# Large media stays out of git: the files are uploaded to the tenant and Slack.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.wav
*.mp3
*.onnx
